    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Paleoagave</b></i> is a genus of flowering plants in the family Asparagaceae. It includes a single species, <i><b>Paleoagave bracteosa</b></i> (synonym <i>Agave bracteosa</i>) which commonly known as <b>spider agave</b> or <b>squid agave</b>. It is native to the Sierra Madre Oriental of northeastern Mexico (spanning the states of Tamaulipas, Coahuila and Nuevo León), where it prefers well-drained and bright but shaded or protected locations, such as under trees or on cliffs or rocky slopes (facing away from the sun)....",
